.TH ZIX 1 "" "zix 0.14.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zix \- pull, stage, rebuild and clean up a NixOS system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zix
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B zix
\fBhelp\fR | \fBversion\fR
.br
.B zix
\fB\-\-completions\fR \fISHELL\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zix
runs the NixOS update cycle against a dotfiles repository: it pulls the
latest changes, optionally updates the flake inputs, stages the changes,
rebuilds the system with \fBnixos\-rebuild switch\fR, deletes old generations
and optionally shows the closure diff.
.PP
Every external command runs as an argv list (no shell), and each step fails
fast: a failed pull, flake update, stage or rebuild aborts before the next
step.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-repo " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to the dotfiles repository. Default: \fB~/.dotfiles\fR. A leading
\fB~\fR is expanded from \fB$HOME\fR.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-hostname " " \fINAME\fR
Hostname used for the flake attribute (\fIPATH\fR#\fINAME\fR). Default:
detected from \fB/proc/sys/kernel/hostname\fR, \fB$HOSTNAME\fR or
\fBgethostname\fR. The rebuild aborts when no hostname can be detected; a run
that skips the rebuild (for example \fB\-\-only diff\fR) does not need it.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep " " \fIN\fR
Generations to keep during cleanup (1\-255). Default: \fB10\fR.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Cap \fBnix\fR \fB\-\-max\-jobs\fR for the rebuild (1\-65535).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cores " " \fIN\fR
Cap \fBnix\fR \fB\-\-cores\fR for the rebuild (1\-65535).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update
Run \fBnix flake update\fR before staging.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-diff
Show the closure diff between the previous and current generation.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Assume yes for every prompt.
.TP
.BI \-\-only " " \fISTEPS\fR
Run only the listed comma-separated steps: \fBpull\fR, \fBflake\fR,
\fBstage\fR, \fBrebuild\fR, \fBcleanup\fR, \fBdiff\fR. \fBupdate\fR is accepted
as an alias for \fBflake\fR. The list wins over \fB\-\-update\fR and
\fB\-\-diff\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print each command instead of executing it. The read-only capability probe of
\fBnixos\-rebuild\fR still runs, so the preview shows the flavour actually
installed.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colours. Colours are also disabled when \fBNO_COLOR\fR is set or
the stream is not a terminal.
.TP
.BI \-\-completions " " \fISHELL\fR
Print the completion script for \fISHELL\fR (\fBbash\fR, \fBzsh\fR or
\fBfish\fR) to standard output and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the help banner.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.PP
Long options also accept \fB\-\-flag=value\fR (\fB\-\-repo=/path\fR,
\fB\-\-only=diff\fR).
.SH STEP SELECTION
Without \fB\-\-only\fR the pipeline is: \fBpull\fR, \fBflake\fR (only with
\fB\-\-update\fR), \fBstage\fR, \fBrebuild\fR, \fBcleanup\fR and \fBdiff\fR
(only with \fB\-\-diff\fR). Declining the staging prompt aborts the run. A
closed stdin is never treated as a confirmation.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or the user aborted at a prompt.
.TP
.B 1
A workflow step failed (pull, stage, rebuild, cleanup, diff), the hostname
could not be detected, or the repository is not a git work tree.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments or configuration.
.TP
.B 141
Standard output was closed early (128 + SIGPIPE).
.PP
A child process killed by signal \fIN\fR yields \fB128\fR + \fIN\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.I NO_COLOR
When non-empty, disables ANSI colours.
.TP
.I TERM
\fBdumb\fR disables ANSI colours.
.TP
.I HOME
Used to expand a leading \fB~\fR in \fB\-\-repo\fR.
.TP
.I HOSTNAME
Fallback hostname source.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.dotfiles
Default repository.
.TP
.I /nix/var/nix/profiles/system
System profile used for generation pruning and the closure diff.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nixos\-rebuild (8),
.BR nix (1),
.BR git (1)
